('orig-dilr-s09-q1', 'DILR', 'Arrangements (linear/circular)', 'MCQ', 'Whose manuscript is the third longest?', 'Book publishing

Five authors A–E submit manuscripts of different lengths. A’s is longer than B’s but shorter than C’s; D’s is shorter than B’s; E’s is longer than C’s. Editing time is proportional to length: the shortest manuscript takes 6 days and the longest 18 days, and the five editing times form an arithmetic progression.', '["D", "C", "B", "A"]'::jsonb, '3', 'The order from shortest is D, B, A, C, E, so A is third longest. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10093, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::arrangements-linear-circular-', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Arrangements (linear/circular)'),
('orig-dilr-s09-q2', 'DILR', 'Arrangements (linear/circular)', 'TITA', 'How many days does C’s manuscript take to edit?', 'Book publishing

Five authors A–E submit manuscripts of different lengths. A’s is longer than B’s but shorter than C’s; D’s is shorter than B’s; E’s is longer than C’s. Editing time is proportional to length: the shortest manuscript takes 6 days and the longest 18 days, and the five editing times form an arithmetic progression.', NULL, '15', 'The times are 6, 9, 12, 15, 18 days for D, B, A, C, E. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10094, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::arrangements-linear-circular-', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Arrangements (linear/circular)'),
('orig-dilr-s09-q3', 'DILR', 'Arrangements (linear/circular)', 'TITA', 'If one editor works through the manuscripts from shortest to longest without a break, after how many days does she finish A’s?', 'Book publishing

Five authors A–E submit manuscripts of different lengths. A’s is longer than B’s but shorter than C’s; D’s is shorter than B’s; E’s is longer than C’s. Editing time is proportional to length: the shortest manuscript takes 6 days and the longest 18 days, and the five editing times form an arithmetic progression.', NULL, '27', '6 (D) + 9 (B) + 12 (A) = 27 days. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'HARD', 10095, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::arrangements-linear-circular-', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Arrangements (linear/circular)'),
('orig-dilr-s10-q1', 'DILR', 'Tables & Caselets', 'TITA', 'How many litres remain in the three reservoirs after the week?', 'Water reservoirs

Three reservoirs X, Y and Z hold 6,000 litres in total. X holds twice as much as Y, and Z holds 500 litres less than X. Over a week, X loses 10%, Y loses 15% and Z loses 20% of its water to evaporation.', NULL, '5125', 'Y = 1300, X = 2600, Z = 2100. Losses: 260 + 195 + 420 = 875, so 5125 litres remain. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10096, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::data-interpretation::tables-caselets', 'DILR › Data Interpretation › Tables & Caselets'),
('orig-dilr-s10-q2', 'DILR', 'Tables & Caselets', 'MCQ', 'Which reservoir loses the most water?', 'Water reservoirs

Three reservoirs X, Y and Z hold 6,000 litres in total. X holds twice as much as Y, and Z holds 500 litres less than X. Over a week, X loses 10%, Y loses 15% and Z loses 20% of its water to evaporation.', '["Y", "Z", "X and Z equally", "X"]'::jsonb, '1', 'Losses: X 260, Y 195, Z 420 litres. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10097, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::data-interpretation::tables-caselets', 'DILR › Data Interpretation › Tables & Caselets'),
('orig-dilr-s10-q3', 'DILR', 'Tables & Caselets', 'MCQ', 'What percentage of the total water is lost?', 'Water reservoirs

