('orig-dilr-s11-q1', 'DILR', 'Tables & Caselets', 'TITA', 'How many tablets are sold in total?', 'Online marketplace

Four sellers A–D sell 1,000 phones and tablets in all. A accounts for 20% of the units, B for 25%, C for 30% and D for the rest. Phones make up 60% of A’s units, 40% of B’s, 50% of C’s and 70% of D’s.', NULL, '455', 'Phones: 120 + 100 + 150 + 175 = 545, so tablets = 455. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10099, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::data-interpretation::tables-caselets', 'DILR › Data Interpretation › Tables & Caselets'),
('orig-dilr-s11-q2', 'DILR', 'Tables & Caselets', 'MCQ', 'Which two sellers sell the same number of tablets?', 'Online marketplace

