('orig-dilr-s12-q1', 'DILR', 'Scheduling & Calendars', 'MCQ', 'If E is in slot 2, which talk is in slot 4?', 'Conference scheduling

Seven talks A–G occupy seven consecutive slots, numbered 1 to 7. A is scheduled before D. B immediately follows E. C is neither first nor last. F is after D. G is before E. A and C are not in adjacent slots.', '["A", "C", "D", "F"]'::jsonb, '0', 'G must be in slot 1 and B in slot 3; the only order that works is G, E, B, A, D, C, F. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10102, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::scheduling-calendars', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Scheduling & Calendars'),
('orig-dilr-s12-q2', 'DILR', 'Scheduling & Calendars', 'TITA', 'If C is in slot 2, in which slot is D?', 'Conference scheduling

Seven talks A–G occupy seven consecutive slots, numbered 1 to 7. A is scheduled before D. B immediately follows E. C is neither first nor last. F is after D. G is before E. A and C are not in adjacent slots.', NULL, '6', 'The only order is G, C, E, B, A, D, F. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10103, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::scheduling-calendars', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Scheduling & Calendars'),
('orig-dilr-s12-q3', 'DILR', 'Scheduling & Calendars', 'MCQ', 'Which of these talks can be scheduled in slot 7?', 'Conference scheduling

Seven talks A–G occupy seven consecutive slots, numbered 1 to 7. A is scheduled before D. B immediately follows E. C is neither first nor last. F is after D. G is before E. A and C are not in adjacent slots.', '["D", "E", "B", "G"]'::jsonb, '2', 'Only B or F can ever be last; D needs F after it, and G and E need B after them. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'HARD', 10104, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::scheduling-calendars', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Scheduling & Calendars'),
('orig-dilr-s13-q1', 'DILR', 'Quant-based LR', 'MCQ', 'In what ratio are X and Y mixed in the first blend?', 'Fuel blend

A fuel station blends petrol grades X (₹96 per litre) and Y (₹108 per litre). The first blend sells at ₹110 per litre at a 10% profit on cost. A second blend mixes the first blend with pure Y in the ratio 3 : 2.', '["3 : 2", "1 : 2", "2 : 1", "1 : 1"]'::jsonb, '2', 'Cost of the blend = 110/1.1 = ₹100. By alligation, X : Y = (108 − 100) : (100 − 96) = 2 : 1. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10105, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::quant-based-lr', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Quant-based LR'),
('orig-dilr-s13-q2', 'DILR', 'Quant-based LR', 'TITA', 'What percentage of the second blend is grade Y?', 'Fuel blend

A fuel station blends petrol grades X (₹96 per litre) and Y (₹108 per litre). The first blend sells at ₹110 per litre at a 10% profit on cost. A second blend mixes the first blend with pure Y in the ratio 3 : 2.', NULL, '60', 'Y = 3 × (1/3) + 2 = 3 parts of 5 = 60%. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10106, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::quant-based-lr', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Quant-based LR'),
('orig-dilr-s13-q3', 'DILR', 'Quant-based LR', 'MCQ', 'What is the cost per litre of the second blend?', 'Fuel blend

A fuel station blends petrol grades X (₹96 per litre) and Y (₹108 per litre). The first blend sells at ₹110 per litre at a 10% profit on cost. A second blend mixes the first blend with pure Y in the ratio 3 : 2.', '["₹102.40", "₹104.00", "₹103.20", "₹100.80"]'::jsonb, '2', '0.4 × 96 + 0.6 × 108 = ₹103.20. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'HARD', 10107, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::quant-based-lr', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Quant-based LR'),
('orig-dilr-s14-q1', 'DILR', 'Tables & Caselets', 'TITA', 'How many loans did branch B make?', 'Library circulation

Four library branches A–D made 1,200 loans: 50% fiction, 30% science and 20% history. Branch A made 25% of the fiction loans, 20% of the science loans and 10% of the history loans; branch B made 30%, 30% and 20% respectively. Branches C and D split the remaining loans in each category equally.', NULL, '336', 'B: 180 fiction + 108 science + 48 history = 336. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10108, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::data-interpretation::tables-caselets', 'DILR › Data Interpretation › Tables & Caselets'),
('orig-dilr-s14-q2', 'DILR', 'Tables & Caselets', 'MCQ', 'Which branch made the most history loans?', 'Library circulation

Four library branches A–D made 1,200 loans: 50% fiction, 30% science and 20% history. Branch A made 25% of the fiction loans, 20% of the science loans and 10% of the history loans; branch B made 30%, 30% and 20% respectively. Branches C and D split the remaining loans in each category equally.', '["B", "C", "C and D equally", "A"]'::jsonb, '2', 'History: A 24, B 48, C 84, D 84. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10109, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::data-interpretation::tables-caselets', 'DILR › Data Interpretation › Tables & Caselets'),
('orig-dilr-s14-q3', 'DILR', 'Tables & Caselets', 'MCQ', 'What percentage of all loans were made by branch A?', 'Library circulation

Four library branches A–D made 1,200 loans: 50% fiction, 30% science and 20% history. Branch A made 25% of the fiction loans, 20% of the science loans and 10% of the history loans; branch B made 30%, 30% and 20% respectively. Branches C and D split the remaining loans in each category equally.', '["25.00%", "22.00%", "20.50%", "18.75%"]'::jsonb, '2', 'A: 150 + 72 + 24 = 246 of 1200 = 20.5%. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'HARD', 10110, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::data-interpretation::tables-caselets', 'DILR › Data Interpretation › Tables & Caselets'),
('orig-dilr-s15-q1', 'DILR', 'Quant-based LR', 'TITA', 'How many users make a purchase?', 'App engagement

A cohort of 2,000 app users is split into low, medium and high daily use in the ratio 5 : 3 : 2. After 30 days, 20% of low users, 50% of medium users and 80% of high users are still active. 40% of the users still active make a purchase, against 5% of the others.', NULL, '387', 'Retained: 200 + 300 + 320 = 820. Buyers: 328 + 5% of 1180 (59) = 387. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10111, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::quant-based-lr', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Quant-based LR'),
('orig-dilr-s15-q2', 'DILR', 'Quant-based LR', 'TITA', 'What percentage of the cohort is still active after 30 days?', 'App engagement

A cohort of 2,000 app users is split into low, medium and high daily use in the ratio 5 : 3 : 2. After 30 days, 20% of low users, 50% of medium users and 80% of high users are still active. 40% of the users still active make a purchase, against 5% of the others.', NULL, '41', '820/2000 = 41%. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10112, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::quant-based-lr', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Quant-based LR'),
('orig-dilr-s15-q3', 'DILR', 'Quant-based LR', 'MCQ', 'What percentage of buyers are still-active users?', 'App engagement

A cohort of 2,000 app users is split into low, medium and high daily use in the ratio 5 : 3 : 2. After 30 days, 20% of low users, 50% of medium users and 80% of high users are still active. 40% of the users still active make a purchase, against 5% of the others.', '["41.00%", "15.25%", "84.75%", "80.00%"]'::jsonb, '2', '328/387 = 84.75%. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'HARD', 10113, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::quant-based-lr', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Quant-based LR'),
('orig-dilr-s16-q1', 'DILR', 'Arrangements (linear/circular)', 'MCQ', 'Who sits opposite B?', 'Circular seating

Eight people A–H sit around a circular table, equally spaced. A sits opposite E. B sits immediately clockwise of A. C sits immediately anticlockwise of E. D is not next to A or E. F sits between G and H, and G is next to A.', '["C", "H", "F", "G"]'::jsonb, '1', 'Going clockwise from A: A, B, D, C, E, H, F, G. B is opposite H. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10114, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::arrangements-linear-circular-', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Arrangements (linear/circular)'),
('orig-dilr-s16-q2', 'DILR', 'Arrangements (linear/circular)', 'MCQ', 'Who sits immediately clockwise of E?', 'Circular seating

Eight people A–H sit around a circular table, equally spaced. A sits opposite E. B sits immediately clockwise of A. C sits immediately anticlockwise of E. D is not next to A or E. F sits between G and H, and G is next to A.', '["D", "C", "H", "F"]'::jsonb, '2', 'E is followed clockwise by H. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10115, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::arrangements-linear-circular-', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Arrangements (linear/circular)'),
('orig-dilr-s16-q3', 'DILR', 'Arrangements (linear/circular)', 'TITA', 'Going clockwise from D to F, how many people sit between them?', 'Circular seating

Eight people A–H sit around a circular table, equally spaced. A sits opposite E. B sits immediately clockwise of A. C sits immediately anticlockwise of E. D is not next to A or E. F sits between G and H, and G is next to A.', NULL, '3', 'C, E and H sit between D and F. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'HARD', 10116, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::arrangements-linear-circular-', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Arrangements (linear/circular)'),
('orig-dilr-s17-q1', 'DILR', 'Games & Tournaments', 'TITA', 'How many points are awarded in the league in total?', 'Sports league

Five clubs A–E play each other twice, so each plays 8 matches. Their records (won–drawn–lost) are: A 6–2–0, B 4–2–2, C 3–4–1, D 1–2–5 and E 0–2–6. A win earns 3 points and a draw 1 point.', NULL, '54', '14 decided matches × 3 + 6 drawn matches × 2 = 54. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10117, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::games-tournaments', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Games & Tournaments'),
('orig-dilr-s17-q2', 'DILR', 'Games & Tournaments', 'MCQ', 'Which club finishes second?', 'Sports league

Five clubs A–E play each other twice, so each plays 8 matches. Their records (won–drawn–lost) are: A 6–2–0, B 4–2–2, C 3–4–1, D 1–2–5 and E 0–2–6. A win earns 3 points and a draw 1 point.', '["D", "B", "C", "B and C equally"]'::jsonb, '1', 'Points: A 20, B 14, C 13, D 5, E 2. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10118, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::games-tournaments', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Games & Tournaments'),
('orig-dilr-s17-q3', 'DILR', 'Games & Tournaments', 'MCQ', 'Under a system of 2 points per win and 1 per draw, what would happen to second place?', 'Sports league

Five clubs A–E play each other twice, so each plays 8 matches. Their records (won–drawn–lost) are: A 6–2–0, B 4–2–2, C 3–4–1, D 1–2–5 and E 0–2–6. A win earns 3 points and a draw 1 point.', '["B would still be second alone", "D would move up to second", "B and C would tie", "C would be second alone"]'::jsonb, '2', 'B: 8 + 2 = 10; C: 6 + 4 = 10, so they would tie for second. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'HARD', 10119, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::games-tournaments', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Games & Tournaments'),
('orig-dilr-s18-q1', 'DILR', 'Tables & Caselets', 'TITA', 'What is the shop’s total revenue in rupees after discounts?', 'Pricing strategy

A shop sells 1,200 units of products P, Q and R in the ratio 3 : 4 : 5. Their list prices are ₹200, ₹250 and ₹160, and they are sold at discounts of 10%, 20% and 15% respectively.', NULL, '202000', 'P: 300 × 180 = 54,000; Q: 400 × 200 = 80,000; R: 500 × 136 = 68,000. Total ₹2,02,000. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10120, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::data-interpretation::tables-caselets', 'DILR › Data Interpretation › Tables & Caselets'),
('orig-dilr-s18-q2', 'DILR', 'Tables & Caselets', 'MCQ', 'Which product brings in the most revenue?', 'Pricing strategy

