('orig-dilr-s18-q3', 'DILR', 'Tables & Caselets', 'MCQ', 'Total discount given is what percentage of the total list value?', 'Pricing strategy

A shop sells 1,200 units of products P, Q and R in the ratio 3 : 4 : 5. Their list prices are ₹200, ₹250 and ₹160, and they are sold at discounts of 10%, 20% and 15% respectively.', '["15.83%", "17.50%", "15.00%", "14.25%"]'::jsonb, '0', 'List value = 60,000 + 1,00,000 + 80,000 = 2,40,000. Discount = 38,000 = 15.83%. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'HARD', 10122, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::data-interpretation::tables-caselets', 'DILR › Data Interpretation › Tables & Caselets'),
('orig-dilr-s19-q1', 'DILR', 'Scheduling & Calendars', 'MCQ', 'Which train leaves at 8:20?', 'Train timetable

Four trains A–D leave a station at 8:00, 8:10, 8:20 and 8:30, one at each time. A leaves before C. B leaves exactly 20 minutes after D. C does not leave last.', '["D", "C", "A", "B"]'::jsonb, '1', 'D and B must be 8:10 and 8:30 (otherwise C is last), leaving A at 8:00 and C at 8:20. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'MODERATE', 10123, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::scheduling-calendars', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Scheduling & Calendars'),
('orig-dilr-s19-q2', 'DILR', 'Scheduling & Calendars', 'MCQ', 'Which train leaves last?', 'Train timetable

