('orig-dilr-s19-q3', 'DILR', 'Scheduling & Calendars', 'TITA', 'If the condition that C does not leave last were removed, how many departure orders would be possible?', 'Train timetable

Four trains A–D leave a station at 8:00, 8:10, 8:20 and 8:30, one at each time. A leaves before C. B leaves exactly 20 minutes after D. C does not leave last.', NULL, '2', 'D 8:00, B 8:20 with A 8:10, C 8:30 also becomes possible. From the CAT 2026 Original Advanced Question Bank (cleaned and verified).', 'HARD', 10125, 'BANK', now(), 'dilr::logical-reasoning::scheduling-calendars', 'DILR › Logical Reasoning › Scheduling & Calendars'),
('orig-dilr-s20-q1', 'DILR', 'Venn diagrams', 'TITA', 'How many people use none of the three services?', 'Survey analysis

